WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.963
It was a dark, starless night. The moon was hidden in the cloudy sky.

2
00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:11.084
Peter crawled on his belly, snakelike, across the ground.

3
00:00:11.085 --> 00:00:15.282
This was one of many useful things the Indians had taught him.

4
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:23.080
Tinker Bell was still too weak to fly and light the way, so Peter had decided not to fly himself.

5
00:00:23.081 --> 00:00:28.486
He knew where he was headed—the pirate ship, the Jolly Roger

6
00:00:28.487 --> 00:00:34.679
! Suddenly, Peter caught sight of the crocodile, which was also creeping in the

7
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:40.094
dark. No other living creature seemed to be awake but the boy and the

8
00:00:40.095 --> 00:00:45.400
crocodile. And they were both after the same prey—Captain

9
00:00:45.401 --> 00:00:51.382
Hook. In the silence of the night, Peter realized something was different about the

10
00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:55.156
crocodile. The clock inside it had finally stopped

11
00:00:55.157 --> 00:00:58.919
ticking. At that moment, Peter had an

12
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:06.251
idea. He was determined to rescue Wendy and the boys, but he was also eager to destroy his

13
00:01:06.252 --> 00:01:12.251
rival. "This time, it’s Hook or me!" he thought with great

14
00:01:12.252 --> 00:01:15.135
excitement. And he started to form a

15
00:01:15.136 --> 00:01:20.055
plan. The Jolly Roger was anchored not far from the shore of Kidd’s

16
00:01:20.056 --> 00:01:27.275
Creek. On board, some of the pirates were sleeping, and others were playing dice and

17
00:01:27.276 --> 00:01:35.645
cards. Even though it was after midnight, Smee sat at the ship’s sewing machine, busily mending the captain’s

18
00:01:35.646 --> 00:01:39.231
clothes. Hook walked the deck deep in

19
00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:43.947
thought. This should have been his moment of triumph. Peter was

20
00:01:43.948 --> 00:01:47.522
dead. The boys were tied up and soon would walk the

21
00:01:47.523 --> 00:01:53.178
plank. And Wendy was his captive. But Hook felt unhappy and

22
00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:56.956
alone. Even among his pirates, Hook was

23
00:01:56.957 --> 00:02:00.525
lonely. They were no better than dogs that obeyed

24
00:02:00.526 --> 00:02:05.180
him. They certainly were not equals who could listen to his

25
00:02:05.181 --> 00:02:12.870
feelings. How cruel fate had been to the captain! Hook hadn’t always been a

26
00:02:12.871 --> 00:02:15.522
pirate. Hook wasn’t even his real

27
00:02:15.523 --> 00:02:20.078
name. Once, he had been a promising young man at a private

28
00:02:20.079 --> 00:02:25.854
school. There he had learned the manners and fancy dress that could have made him a gentleman.

29
00:02:25.855 --> 00:02:31.243
But he had wanted fame, and evil had taken hold of him.

30
00:02:31.244 --> 00:02:34.491
"What good are all my evil triumphs in the end?

31
00:02:34.492 --> 00:02:38.423
No little children love me," he thought.

32
00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:42.195
It was strange that he should suddenly think of these things.

33
00:02:42.196 --> 00:02:46.614
Maybe it was the sound of Smee’s sewing machine.

34
00:02:46.615 --> 00:02:51.076
Even though he was a pirate, old Smee was lovable.

35
00:02:51.077 --> 00:02:56.056
There was not a child on board the ship who did not already love Smee.

36
00:02:56.057 --> 00:03:06.303
He had given Wendy a cloak to keep warm, and Michael had even tried on his glasses.

37
00:03:06.304 --> 00:03:10.825
"What does Smee have that I do not?" wondered Hook.

38
00:03:10.826 --> 00:03:14.950
He needed to do something wicked to feel better again.

39
00:03:14.951 --> 00:03:23.364
Standing a little taller, Hook shouted to his men, "Are all the boys chained so they cannot fly away?"

40
00:03:23.365 --> 00:03:27.011
"Ay, ay," they answered.

41
00:03:27.012 --> 00:03:30.736
"Then bring them up," he ordered.

42
00:03:30.737 --> 00:03:34.617
The poor prisoners were dragged from the hold below.

43
00:03:34.618 --> 00:03:38.177
The eight boys stood in a line in front of him.

44
00:03:38.178 --> 00:03:41.060
"Six of you will walk the plank tonight.

45
00:03:41.061 --> 00:03:48.155
But I will keep two to be my cabin boys. Who wishes to serve me?"

46
00:03:48.156 --> 00:03:53.481
The boys were silent. Finally Tootles spoke up.

47
00:03:53.482 --> 00:03:58.606
"Sir, I don’t think my mother would like me to be a pirate.

48
00:03:58.607 --> 00:04:02.618
Would your mother like you to be a pirate, Slightly?"

49
00:04:02.619 --> 00:04:12.776
"I don’t think so," Slightly answered sadly, as if he wished it were otherwise. The other boys agreed.

50
00:04:12.777 --> 00:04:17.487
Hook was angry. He looked directly at John.

51
00:04:17.488 --> 00:04:22.327
"You seem to have a little more courage, boy," he said.

52
00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:25.089
"Did you ever want to be a pirate?"

53
00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:31.708
John became thoughtful. "Yes, there was a time when I wanted to be a pirate."

54
00:04:31.709 --> 00:04:37.439
Then he looked around at his friends. "But that was long ago."

55
00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.655
"Then go to your doom!" Hook roared.

56
00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:45.718
To his men he said, "Get the plank ready!

57
00:04:45.719 --> 00:04:54.259
And bring up their mother to watch!"

